+## Pi task snapshot
+
+`tools/pi-worker-task.mjs prepare --config /absolute/trusted.json --output /absolute/nonexistent-task.mjs` creates a self-contained task snapshot for the existing runner. The trusted config pins the Pi SDK and Node paths, opaque host auth-file path, baseline Git profile/reference map, brief text, mode (`offline` or explicitly authorized `real`), protected check command, and expected mutable paths. Preparation reads methodology bytes from the pinned local Git objects and embeds all inputs in the generated script; subsequent task execution does not reread that config or checkout. Pass the generated script to `worker-lifecycle.mjs launch` as `--task-script`, with the usual 120000 ms outer timeout. Offline mode validates SDK/session/tool setup without a provider prompt. Real mode requests only `openai-codex/gpt-6-luna` at `high`, with a 12-tool-call cap and 110-second inner deadline; process completion is not product acceptance. This narrow integration is not a general sandbox, coordinator, recovery mechanism, or claim of native Pi teardown.
